follow-up after Anna’s emails and tracker gaps.</p><p>**Behaviour patterns**</p><p>- Positive: increased contact/keeping-in-touch discipline improving pipeline and results.</p><p>- Risk: protection activity displaced by mortgage workload; workflow staging improvised where process doesn’t fit.</p><p>**Accountability concerns**</p><p>- Admin-owned stage correction outstanding (27 January lead status).</p><p>- Need clearer ownership allocation for nurture/property-search client calls (Sean to call where Paul isn’t).</p><p>**Where management support is required**</p><p>- **Bob** to escalate if NatWest / Juliana resists holding the passport case open.</p><p>- Process/workflow feedback loop (renewal/keeping-in-touch path) to reduce inconsistent staging until migration.</p><p>**Trend insight:** **Improving overall** — strong revenue and pipeline trajectory, but **protection focus + CRM accuracy** remain the key performance risks.</p><p>---</p><p>## 12) Master Action List (only evidenced actions)</p><p>| Action | Client / Area | Owner | Deadline | Risk if not done |</p><p>|---|---|---|---|---|</p><p>| Prevent NatWest auto-closure: upload holding PDF re passport renewal; instruct “do not cancel”; escalate to Bob if needed | Purchase + Remortgage (NatWest, submitted 6th; passport expired) | Sean + Paul (Bob if escalation) | 2026-03-18 | Case auto-closes; client loses rate; reputational damage; pipeline drop |</p><p>| Confirm corrected ID accepted and log next steps in CRM | Case submitted 12th (ID thumb over signature) | Sean | 2026-03-18 | Continued doc churn; SLA drift; avoidable delays |</p><p>| Confirm lender receipt/portal update and log CRM note + next task | Angie Ray (maternity payslip) | Sean | 2026-03-18 | Case stalls; missed follow-up; timeline slips |</p><p>| Monitor valuation and chase offer issuance post-valuation; update CRM | Sarah Budge | Sean | 2026-03-19 | Offer delayed; pipeline slippage |</p><p>| Chase valuation outcome and progress underwriting; keep CRM