ss**; NatWest delays creating time/rate risk.</p><p>### What is working</p><p>- Strong February lead-to-application conversion (24.2%) with offers and a completion.</p><p>- Mortgage pipeline is active (9 cases in progress) and projected income visibility has improved.</p><p>- Workflow overdue load is materially reduced (1 day overdue item referenced).</p><p>### Identified risks</p><p>- **Protection off pace in March** and an appointment planned for **2026-03-18** was missed/rebook needed.  </p><p>- **NatWest auto-closure/rate loss risk** on purchase + remortgage case submitted **6th** (passport expired).  </p><p>- **CRM accuracy risk:** lead last added **27 January** is booked but still in **Created** (stage not updated).  </p><p>- **Lead leakage risk:** **Borders** not using booking link; slower engagement and more chasing.</p><p>### Cases Requiring Attention</p><p>- **NatWest purchase + remortgage (submitted 6th):** passport expired; prevent auto-closure and instruct “do not cancel”. **Owners:** Sean + Paul (Bob if escalation needed).  </p><p>- **Angie Ray:** confirm maternity payslip received/portal updated; log next steps. **Owner:** Sean.  </p><p>- **Sarah Budge:** valuation on **2026-03-19**; chase offer post-valuation. **Owner:** Sean.  </p><p>- **Brianna Kennedy (NatWest):** valuation on **2026-03-19**; chase outcome and underwriting. **Owner:** Sean.  </p><p>- **Emily:** down-valuation to **£700k** and underwriting questions; reassess PT vs 80% LTV remortgage and document responses. **Owner:** Paul.  </p><p>- **Charlie Rintoul:** HSBC details not pulling through; validate data and log next step. **Owner:** Paul.  </p><p>- **Dunlop:** protection review rescheduled from **2026-03-18**; rebook and log. **Owner:** Paul.</p><p>### Revenue and Pipeline Risks (only where discussed)</p><p>- Protection slippage risks pushing written income into April if not placed/recorded promptly (incl. **£3.5k** pending).</p><p>- NatWest delays/auto-closure risk can cause rate loss and pipeline drop-off.</p><p>### Focus for Next Week</p><p>- Rebuild protection momentum: rebook missed protection appointment and lock protection reviews for cases at/near offer.</p><p>- Tighten CRM hygiene: no booked leads left in **Created**; ensure owner/next step/task dates are set.</p><p>- Reduce lead leakage: Borders to use booking link so leads book directly into your diary.</p><p>- Aggressive milestone chasing on NatWest/valuation gates to prevent SLA drift and rate loss.</p><p>### Agreed Actions</p><p>| Action | Owner | Deadline |</p><p>|---|---|---|</p><p>| Prevent NatWest auto-closure; upload holding note; instruct “do not cancel”; escalate to Bob if needed | Sean + Paul (Bob if escalation) | 2026-03-18 |</p><p>| Confirm corrected ID accepted and set next steps | Sean | 2026-03-18 |</p><p>| Confirm Angie Ray doc receipt + portal update; log CRM note and next task | Sean | 2026-03-18 |</p><p>| Monitor Sarah Budge valuation and chase offer | Sean | 2026-03-19 |</p><p>| Chase Brianna Kennedy valuation outcome and underwriting | Sean | 2026-03-19 |</p><p>| Update 27 January lead to correct stage (Appointment Booked) and update notes | Anna | 2026-03-19 |</p><p>| Deliver desk market update and send follow-up email summary | Paul | 2026-03-19 |</p><p>| Email booking link to Amy for Borders to use for all referrals | Paul | 2026-03-19 |</p><p>| Confirm booking link routes correctly into Paul’s diary | Ops/Systems | 2026-03-19 |</p><p>| Rebook and log Dunlop protection review | Paul | 2026-03-20 |</p><p>| Place and correctly record the £3.5k protection case | Paul | 2026-03-20 |</p><p>| Review and correctly dispose the 2 Unable to Place leads | Paul | 2026-03-21 |</p><p>| Audit March Created leads for owner/next step/dated task | Paul | 2026-03-21 |</p><p>| Fix HSBC details retrieval blocker for Charlie Rintoul and log next step | Paul | 2026-03-25 |</p><p>| Rebook Jess training time via John | Bob | 2026-03-25 |</p><p>If circumstances change during the week,